    "body": "Fixes #60981\n\n## Purpose\n\nIn `vllm/v1/spec_decode/ngram_proposer_gpu.py:340`, `NgramProposerGPU.propose` hardcodes `assert num_speculative_tokens == self.k`. When dynamic speculative decoding is configured (e.g. via `num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size`), the scheduler dynamically requests fewer speculative tokens under load (including K=0 or sub-step K < k). This caused an immediate `AssertionError` and killed the worker process (`EngineDeadError`).\n\nThis PR:\n1. Relaxes the assertion to `assert 0 <= num_speculative_tokens <= self.k` (matching the CPU implementation in `ngram_proposer.py:38`).\n2. Safely handles `num_speculative_tokens == 0`: scatters newly sampled tokens to `token_ids_gpu` to maintain historical context, then returns empty tensors `[batch_size, 0]` without running the kernel.\n3. When `num_speculative_tokens < self.k`, slices proposed draft tokens to `num_speculative_tokens` and clamps `num_valid_draft_tokens`.\n4. Adds unit tests covering full-step K, sub-step K, K=0 context preservation, and multi-tier dynamic schedules.\n\n## Why this is not a duplicate\n\n- `gh pr list --search \"60981 in:body\"` and `gh pr list --search \"ngram_proposer_gpu\"` returned 0 matching open PRs.\n- The issue was filed on 2026-10-10 and had no linked PRs or assignee.\n\n## Test Plan & Evidence\n\n### 1. Regression Unit Tests\nRan on an NVIDIA L20 GPU:\n```bash\npytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_ngram.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_dynamic_sd.py -v\n```\nResult: `20 passed in 15.50s`.\n\n### 2. End-to-End Real Model Smoke Test on Hardware\n- **Hardware**: 1× NVIDIA L20 (48GB)\n- **Model**: `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B` (`Qwen3ForCausalLM`, bf16)\n- **Speculative Configuration**:\n  ```python\n  speculative_config = {\n      \"method\": \"ngram_gpu\",\n      \"prompt_lookup_min\": 2,\n      \"prompt_lookup_max\": 5,\n      \"num_speculative_tokens\": 4,\n      \"num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size\": [[1, 16, 4], [17, 256, 0]],\n  }\n  ```\n\n**Before Fix:**\nSending 24 concurrent requests triggered scheduler K=0, crashing immediately with:\n```text\n(EngineCore pid=3260083) ERROR [core.py:1507]   File \"vllm/v1/spec_decode/ngram_proposer_gpu.py\", line 340, in propose\n(EngineCore pid=3260083) ERROR [core.py:1507]     assert num_speculative_tokens == self.k\n(EngineCore pid=3260083) ERROR [core.py:1507] AssertionError\nvllm.v1.engine.exceptions.EngineDeadError: Engine core process died.\n```\n\n**After Fix:**\n- Batch size 1 (K=4): Completed in 0.12s with expected draft speedup.\n- Batch size 24 (K=0 -> K=4 transition): All 24 requests completed successfully in 0.48s with valid token generation (0 failures).\n- Multi-tier Schedule (`[[1, 8, 4], [9, 16, 2], [17, 256, 0]]`): 20 concurrent requests completed seamlessly across all tiers (K=0 -> K=2 -> K=4).\n\nAI assistance was used to analyze the codebase, draft the regression test, and format this PR description.\r\n",
